  'dom.dom-pool.alloc': 'Allocates a new node (with parallel names/vals slots) and returns its index'
  'dom.dom-pool.append': 'Appends child to the end of parent\'s child list (an existing parent is detached first)'
  'dom.dom-pool.attr-edge-at': 'Returns the edge index of the node\'s i-th attribute in document order; -1 = out of range'
  'dom.dom-pool.collect-class': `
Collects the indices of elements in node's subtree whose class attribute contains the word
cls
`
  'dom.dom-pool.collect-tag': `
Collects the indices of elements in node's subtree whose tag name is want (star=true means
every element)
`
  'dom.dom-pool.detach': 'Detaches child from its parent, keeping the child list consistent'
  'dom.dom-pool.find-attr': 'Finds the edge index of the node\'s name attribute; -1 means it does not exist'
  'dom.dom-pool.find-id-node': `
Recursively searches node's subtree for an element whose id attribute equals id; -1 = not
found
`
  'dom.dom-pool.html-add-text': 'Decodes s[from..to) by HTML entity rules and appends it to parent as a text node'
  'dom.dom-pool.html-bogus-comment': 'Any other content starting with \'<!\' up to \'>\' is kept as a comment'
  'dom.dom-pool.html-parse-attr': `
Parses an HTML attribute (unquoted values supported); for duplicate attributes the first one
wins
`
  'dom.dom-pool.html-parse-close-name': 'Parses \'</name\' and returns the position after \'>\' plus the lowercase tag name'
  'dom.dom-pool.html-parse-comment': 'Parses <!--...-->, tolerating EOF'
  'dom.dom-pool.html-parse-doc': 'Parses a whole HTML document (never fails) and returns the document root index'
  'dom.dom-pool.html-parse-open': `
Parses a start tag and appends the element to cur
Returns np = the next position, el = the element index, and mode:
0 = an illegal '<' (already treated as text), 1 = an ordinary element (the caller pushes it),
2 = void or self-closing, 3 = raw text already consumed
`
  'dom.dom-pool.html-parse-pi': '\'<?...>\' (HTML treats this as a bogus comment; here it is kept as a PI node)'
  'dom.dom-pool.html-set-attr-once': `
Sets the attribute only when it does not already exist (for duplicate HTML attributes the
first one wins)
`
  'dom.dom-pool.init': 'Initialises the node pool (the heap vec must be initialised before pushing safely)'
  'dom.dom-pool.insert-before': `
Inserts node before ref in parent (appends to the end when ref is illegal or is not a child of
parent)
`
  'dom.dom-pool.parse-doctype-node': `
Parses <!DOCTYPE ...> (including an internal subset and quoted strings); shared by XML and
HTML
Content is stored verbatim (entities are not decoded); the name is the first word after '!'
`
