  'int.to-str': `
converts an integer to a string (a union-type method covering every integer type)
the transpiler resolves i64.to-str() and friends to int.to-str()
it uses arithmetic directly, avoiding the int -> u64 conversion problem
note: it does not take the absolute value of negatives (0 - n overflows when n = i64.MIN);
instead it applies srem/sdiv to the negative value (truncating toward zero) and maps the negative remainder into [0, 9]
