  'math.pow': `
⚠️ known limitations (differences from C pow, all at extreme edges):
1. When |y| > 2^63 the f64-to-i64 conversion overflows and the parity test is wrong, so the sign of inf can flip.
At that point mag is already inf/0, so only the sign is affected.
2. When x==0.0 and y<0, C pow returns +inf whereas this implementation returns 0.0 (following the old behaviour).
`
  'math.pow-int': `
pow: integer power a^n (n >= 0) — works for every integer type
Uses fast exponentiation, O(log n)
⚠️ not moved into math: the name collides with std/math.no's pow (the f64 power function),
and one module cannot hold two pow definitions; this is the single exception to the rule that function-form APIs live in math.
`
  'math.rotate-left': `
[]num.zero = () {
i = 0
for i < .len() {
.[i] = 0
i = i + 1
}
}
═══════════════════════════════════════════════
bit operations (built-in)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════
rotate-left: rotates an integer left by n bits (mapped onto ARM64 ROR via llvm.fshl)
