  'number.exp-f64': `
Exponential and logarithm (f64/f32 methods)
exp-f64: free-function form (takes x as an argument instead of a method receiver).
Serves as the single implementation behind f64.exp / cbrt / sinh / cosh / f32.exp.
Note: Nolang currently has a codegen bug for method calls on named local variables (e.g. t.exp()) that picks up the outer receiver, so every indirect call to exp goes through this free function to sidestep it.
`
