  'number.u64.from-bits': 'the inverse of f64.to-bits (bitcast i64->double), implemented by native LLVM.'
  'number.u64.sqrt': 'u64 (its range exceeds i64, so it needs an independent same-width implementation)'
  'number.u64.to-f64': 'unsigned integer to float'
  'number.u64.to-str': `
converts a u64 to a string (a direct Nolang implementation: the backend has no native u64 formatter,
so the decimal loop of the former math.u64-to-str is inlined into the method body, replacing the deleted function)
`
