  'process.parent-pid': 'gets the parent process ID (a static method)'
  'process.pid-of': 'pid: gets the child process ID'
  'process.process-dup2': 'duplicates a file descriptor'
  'process.process-exec': `
replaces the current process
Calls execlp(program, program, arg, NULL)
Only returns on failure
`
  'process.process-exec-shell': `
runs a command string through sh -c (replacing the current process)
cmd: the full command string
Only returns an errno on failure
`
  'process.process-fork': `
forks the current process
returns 0 = child, >0 = parent (the child PID), -1 = error
`
  'process.process-getppid': 'gets the parent process ID'
  'process.process-kill': 'sends a signal to a process'
  'process.process-pipe': `
creates a pipe
returns the packed value (read_fd << 32) | write_fd
`
  'process.process-shell': `
alternative:
out, stderr, code, err = process.cmd('ls', args, '', '', env, 5000, false)  ; full featured
pid = process.spawn(cmd)                                        ; non-blocking
status = process.wait(pid)                                      ; returns the real exit code
`
  'process.process-system': 'runs a shell command'
  'process.process-waitpid': `
waits for a child process
returns the exit code (WEXITSTATUS)
`
  'process.process-waitpid-nohang': `
non-blocking wait for a child process (WNOHANG)
Returns -1 while the child is still running, its exit code once it has exited, and -1 on error.
Used by the timeout watchdog for polling.
`
  'process.read': `
reads data from the child's stdout
returns read-n = the number of bytes actually read
`
  'process.read-all': `
reads all of the child's stdout output
returns content = the data read, n = the number of bytes read
`
  'process.read-line': `
reads one line from the child's stdout
returns line ?str: ok = the line, nil = EOF or error
`
  'process.shell': `
runs a shell command string and waits for it to finish (spawn plus wait)
cmd: the full command string (executed through sh -c)
returns code = the exit code (0 = success, >0 = the command failed, 127 = exec failed, -1 = fork failed)
`
  'process.shell-quote': `
POSIX single-quote escaping — wraps any string in a single-quoted literal that a shell (sh -c) can safely parse a second time.
An embedded single quote becomes the four-character sequence '\'' (closing quote, escaped quote, opening quote).
Background: cmd()'s general branch runs the assembled command line through process-exec-shell, and the old implementation
joined arguments with bare spaces, losing argument boundaries (an arg containing spaces or quotes was re-tokenised by the shell). This function fixes that defect.
`
  'process.spawn': `
creates a child process running a command string
cmd: the full command string (executed through sh -c)
returns pid > 0 = parent (the child PID), -1 = error
`
  'process.start': `
creates a child process and runs a command (a one-argument convenience method)
program: the program to run
arg: the argument passed to it
returns ok = true = success
`
  'process.start-with-opts': `
run: starts a child process (a low-level instance method; it does not wait or read output)
program   : the program to run (searched on PATH)
args      : the argument list passed to it
dir       : the working directory; empty = inherit the parent's
input     : content written to the child's stdin; empty = no stdin
merge-err : true = merge stderr into stdout
returns ok = true = success; on success it sets .pid/.stdout-fd/.stdin-fd/.running
`
  'process.terminate': `
sends SIG-TERM
returns ok = true = success
`
  'process.wait': `
waits for the child process to finish
returns status = the exit status (WEXITSTATUS)
`
  'process.wait-2': `
waits for the given child process to finish
pid: the child process ID
returns status = the exit status (WEXITSTATUS)
`
  'process.wait-nohang': `
non-blocking wait (polling)
returns status ?i64: ok = the child has finished (its exit status), nil = still running
`
  'process.win-close-handle': 'closes a Windows handle (CloseHandle)'
  'process.win-create-pipe': `
creates an anonymous pipe (CreatePipe)
returns the packed value (read_handle << 32) | write_handle, 0 = failure
`
  'process.win-create-process': `
creates a child process (CreateProcessA)
cmdline: the full command-line string
dir: the working directory (empty = inherit)
stdin-handle, stdout-handle, stderr-handle: the standard-stream handles (0 = inherit from the parent)
returns (proc-handle, status): proc-handle>0 = success, 0 = failure
`
  'process.win-get-exit-code': `
gets a process's exit code (GetExitCodeProcess)
returns exit-code ?i64: nil means it is still running
`
  'process.win-get-std-handle': `
gets a standard handle (GetStdHandle)
which: 0=stdin, 1=stdout, 2=stderr
`
  'process.win-read-pipe': `
reads data from a pipe/handle (ReadFile)
returns (data, n): n = the number of bytes read, -1 = error
`
  'process.win-terminate-process': 'terminates a process (TerminateProcess)'
  'process.win-wait-process': `
waits for a process to finish (WaitForSingleObject)
timeout-ms: the timeout in milliseconds (0 = wait forever)
returns 0 = timed out, 1 = it has exited, -1 = error
