  'str.to-str': `
The generic []t.to-str / [n]t.to-str template calls `.[i].to-str()` on each element; when the element type is str it lands here. std had no such method before, so `['a','b'].to-str()` failed at build time with `unknown callee str.to-str` (generated from the _xstr.to-str forwarding stub).
str is immutable, so returning itself is enough (value semantics: the underlying buffer is shared, not copied).
`
