  'yaml.yaml-parser.looks-like-map-entry': 'Whether this line has a top-level \': \', a trailing \':\', or an explicit key \'? \''
  'yaml.yaml-parser.merge-into': 'Handles the merge key << (a mapping or a sequence of mappings)'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.merge-one': `
Merges the entries of one mapping into keys/vals (existing keys are not overwritten)
Note: the MIR backend forbids moving an input vec directly into another vec (borrow and
ownership protection), so the elements are copied one by one instead of writing ok-keys = keys.
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.newline': 'Consumes one newline (\\n or \\r\\n)'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-alias': 'Parses the alias *name'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-block': 'Parses a block-context node (the current position is the node\'s start column)'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-block-indented': 'Parses the following, more deeply indented lines as a value'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-block-map': 'Parses a block mapping'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-block-scalar': 'Parses the block scalars | and >'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-block-seq': 'Parses a block sequence'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-docs': 'Parses every document'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-document': 'Parses one document and returns the root node index'
